---
/** City/MUD water vs. a private well: who to call for what. */
---

<section class="section section--soft" aria-labelledby="ws-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="ws-h">City water or a well?</h2>
    <div class="ws">
      <div>
        <h3>City or utility district</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Main shut-off at the meter or curb box</li>
          <li>A moving meter with taps off means a leak</li>
          <li>Water quality is in your provider's annual report</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Private well</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Shut water off at the pump's breaker</li>
          <li>A pump running with taps off means a leak</li>
          <li>Pressure tank and switch: plumber. Pump in the well: well pump installer</li>
          <li>Test the water before buying treatment</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .ws { display: grid; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .ws > div { background: #fff; border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; border: 1px dashed var(--accent); }
  .ws ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .ws li { margin: .3rem 0; }
  @media (min-width: 46rem) { .ws { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
</style>
